===Noun===
{{en-plural noun}}

# {{plural of|en|fisticuff}}
# {{lb|en|plurale tantum|informal}} An [[impromptu]] fight with the [[fist]]s, usually between only two people.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1686|author={{w|Nathaniel Johnston}}|chapter=III: That the People are not the Original of Authority and Government|title=The Excellency of Monarchical Government, Eſpecially of the Engliſh Monarchy {{...}}|location=London|publisher=T. B. for Robert Clavel|page={{gbooks|oaM-AQAAMAAJ|19|Fisticuffs}}|passage=So he obſerves that all ſimple Governments are apt to ſome evil that is peculiar and conſequential to their Nature, as he inſtanceth in a Kingdom changed into Monarchy abſolute, by which he means that which we now call Tyranny; Ariſtocracy into Oligarchy, and Democracy into Beſtial Chirocracy, when the Seditious of people prevail more by '''Fiſticuffs''' than reaſon: {{...}}}}
#* '''1881''', [[w:Robert Louis Stevenson|Robert Louis Stevenson]], ''Virginibus Puerisque, and Other Papers'', "[[s:Virginibus_Puerisque#CHAPTER_I_-_.22VIRGINIBUS_PUERISQUE.22|Virginibus Puerisque]],"
#*: People who share a cell in the Basti[l]le {{...}} if they do not immediately fall to '''fisticuffs''', will find some possible ground of compromise.
#* '''1890''', [[w:Edmondo de Amicis|Edmondo de Amicis]] translated by Caroline Tilton, ''Holland and Its People'', [[s:Holland and its People/Chapter XII|Chapter XII]]
#*: {{...}}, his head all scarred with the sticks and '''fisticuffs''' which he had got in the taverns at Utrecht, {{...}}
# {{lb|en|plurale tantum|sports|dated}} [[bare|Bare]]-[[knuckle]]d [[boxing]], a form of boxing done without boxing [[glove]]s or similar padding.
#* {{RQ:Dickens Edwin Drood|chapter=[[s:The Mystery of Edwin Drood/Chapter XVII|Chapter XVII]]|text=In his college days of athletic exercises, Mr. Crisparkle had known professors of the Noble Art of '''fisticuffs''', {{...}}}}

